  "merits": "Many reports give great rewards for visiting these two Imams. Visiting Imam Musa al-Kazim (a.s.) is like visiting the Prophet (s.a.w.a.); another report adds Imam Ali (a.s.); a third likens it to visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.); and a fourth promises Paradise to whoever visits him. Ibn Shahrashub cites al-Khatib al-Baghdadi's Tarikh Baghdad that Ali ibn Khallal would go to Imam Musa (a.s.) whenever a hardship struck him and ask Allah by him, and Allah always relieved it. He also told of a woman hurrying to the Imam's tomb because her son had been imprisoned; a man mocked her that her son would die in prison, and she answered that she asked Allah, by the one who was killed in prison, to show His power. Her son was released at once, and the mocker's son was arrested for his crime.\n\nShaykh al-Saduq reports that Ibrahim ibn Uqbah wrote to Imam Ali al-Naqi (a.s.) asking which was better, visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) or visiting Imam al-Kazim and Imam al-Jawad (a.s.). The Imam wrote back: \"Abu Abdillah (al-Husayn) comes first, and this one is more comprehensive and greater in reward.\"\n\nSome forms of ziyarat at this shrine are shared by the two Imams, like this one, and others belong to each Imam alone ([Imam al-Kazim](AH2), [Imam al-Jawad](AH5)). The farewell is the one Shaykh al-Tusi records in Tahdhib al-Ahkam.\n\nShaykh Abbas al-Qummi adds here the story of Hajj Ali al-Baghdadi, which his teacher Mirza Husayn al-Nuri recorded in al-Najm al-Thaqib and Jannat al-Ma'wa. On a Thursday, after visiting the two Imams and paying his khums to Shaykh Muhammad Hasan Al Yasin in Kazimayn, Hajj Ali set out for Baghdad. On the way a sayyid in a green turban met him, called him by his name, and told him to go back, for it was the eve of Friday. He called the scholars to whom Hajj Ali had paid his khums \"our deputies\" and said what he had paid was accepted. As they walked back, a river and fruit trees out of season ran beside them, which he said accompany every one of their followers who visits their grandfather. He confirmed that worship without loyalty to Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) earns no reward, that visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) on the eve of Friday is a security from the Fire, and that Imam al-Reza (a.s.) would come to the aid, in his grave, of a pilgrim who had eaten for fifteen days at the Imam's guesthouse. At the shrine he recited the permission and greetings for Hajj Ali, who could not read; when he reached the Imam of the Age he told him to greet him, and returned the greeting himself. At the tomb, asked for the best ziyarat, he said it is [Ziyarat Aminullah](G2) and recited it, then visited Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) with [Ziyarat Warith](G6). When the call to the Maghrib prayer came, he told Hajj Ali to join the congregation, and after the prayer he could not be found. Only then did Hajj Ali realise that he had been with Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.); Shaykh Muhammad Hasan told him to keep it secret."
